##DESCRIPTION
##  Algebra problem: linear inequality
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## tcao , PAID on 11-24-2003

## DBsubject(Algebra)
## DBchapter(Linear equations and functions)
## DBsection(Linear inequalities)
## Date(6/3/2002)
## MLT(nINlinINn)
## Level(3)
## TitleText1('Precalculus')
## AuthorText1('Stewart, Redlin, Watson')
## EditionText1('3')
## Section1('1.7')
## Problem1('57')
## KEYWORDS('algebra', 'linear inequality')
DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Interval');

$a = random(1, 20, 1);
$b = random(1, 20, 1);
$c = -$a + 5;

$left  = $a + $b - 5;
$right = $a + $b;

$int = Compute("[$left,$right)");
BEGIN_PGML
The solution of the linear inequality
[``` -[$a] < [$b] - x \le [$c] ```]
is [_]{$int}

*Write the answer in interval notation.*

[@ helpLink('intervals'); @]*
  
END_PGML
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
[```
\begin{aligned}
-[$a] < [$b] - x & \leq [$c] \\
-[$a]-[$b] < -x  & \leq [$c]-[$b] \\
[@ -$a-$b @] < -x & \leq [$c-$b] \qquad \text{multiply by $-1$} \\
[$a+$b] > x & \geq [$b-$c] 
\end{aligned}```]

So the interval is [``[$int]``].
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();        # This should be the last executable line in the problem.